Document Studio 0.2.7 bundles a modified EigenPal 2.25.0 renderer under Apache-2.0.
The inline drawing spacer now contributes to the shaped text paint cursor, avoiding
double horizontal advance beside pictures. Lines starting with a drawing use that
atom's advance start as the paint origin instead of the first text span. Source commit:
ff8242b025c8487c2309027ac65d7e51a14be7f4, packages/core/src/output/semantic-paint.ts.
The checked downstream modification is in scripts/docx-paint-patch.mjs;
dist/native-patch.json in engine-docx records the pinned source digest.

Document Studio 0.2.17 bundles a modified @rhwp/editor 0.8.6 bootstrap under MIT.
The initialization path accepts cancellation while waiting for iframe load,
transport negotiation, native readiness and initial chrome setup. It releases
the frame, event listeners, timers and transport when cancelled. The checked
downstream modification is scripts/rhwp-lifecycle-patch.mjs; engine-rhwp's
dist/native-patch.json records the pinned input digest. RHWP copyright and MIT
license terms are retained in dist/licenses. The Rust/WASM binary is unchanged.

The fixtures are original synthetic documents generated by this project.
They contain no customer or government documents.

dist/licenses/ contains retained third-party notices and a dependency inventory.
The Rust inventory conservatively includes optional/native-only dependencies
from the pinned upstream Cargo.lock; it is not a WASM linker trace. Upstream
MIT blank-document seed and fallback serialization resources remain part of
the RHWP WASM distribution. Its source/license attribution is retained.
Where an archive omits standalone license files, the inventory preserves its
license declaration, original authors/headers, and the selected standard terms.
Document Studio 0.2.6 extends the pinned MIT-licensed RHWP JavaScript runtime
with native snapshot grouping for formatting presets. The upstream source
files and Rust/WASM binary are unchanged. The build-time extension is in
packages/engine-rhwp/native-history-plugin.mjs; the distributed provenance
records its SHA-256. Upstream copyright and license notices are retained.
